{"assets":["/statement-assets/de15ade2c0942d62b3870a15bbc8c0a3814d7bef44f1988022a4f164db62dafe.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1993","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Xor-Grid Problem"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given a matrix $$$a$$$ of size $$$n \\times m$$$, each cell of which contains a non-negative integer. The integer lying at the intersection of the $$$i$$$-th row and the $$$j$$$-th column of the matrix is called $$$a_{i,j}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's define $$$f(i)$$$ and $$$g(j)$$$ as the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exclusive_or"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"XOR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of all integers in the $$$i$$$-th row and the $$$j$$$-th column, respectively. In one operation, you can either: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select any row $$$i$$$, then assign $$$a_{i,j} := g(j)$$$ for each $$$1 \\le j \\le m$$$; or "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select any column $$$j$$$, then assign $$$a_{i,j} := f(i)$$$ for each $$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/de15ade2c0942d62b3870a15bbc8c0a3814d7bef44f1988022a4f164db62dafe.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An example of applying an operation on column $$$2$$$ of the matrix."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this example, as we apply an operation on column $$$2$$$, all elements in this column are changed: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_{1,2} := f(1) = a_{1,1} \\oplus a_{1,2} \\oplus a_{1,3} \\oplus a_{1,4} = 1 \\oplus 1 \\oplus 1 \\oplus 1 = 0$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_{2,2} := f(2) = a_{2,1} \\oplus a_{2,2} \\oplus a_{2,3} \\oplus a_{2,4} = 2 \\oplus 3 \\oplus 5 \\oplus 7 = 3$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_{3,2} := f(3) = a_{3,1} \\oplus a_{3,2} \\oplus a_{3,3} \\oplus a_{3,4} = 2 \\oplus 0 \\oplus 3 \\oplus 0 = 1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_{4,2} := f(4) = a_{4,1} \\oplus a_{4,2} \\oplus a_{4,3} \\oplus a_{4,4} = 10 \\oplus 11 \\oplus 12 \\oplus 16 = 29$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can apply the operations any number of times. Then, we calculate the $$$\\textit{beauty}$$$ of the final matrix by summing the absolute differences between all pairs of its adjacent cells."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"More formally, $$$\\textit{beauty}(a) = \\sum|a_{x,y} - a_{r,c}|$$$ for all cells $$$(x, y)$$$ and $$$(r, c)$$$ if they are adjacent. Two cells are considered adjacent if they share a side."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the minimum $$$\\textit{beauty}$$$ among all obtainable matrices."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 250$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, m \\le 15$$$) — the number of rows and columns of $$$a$$$, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next $$$n$$$ lines, each containing $$$m$$$ integers $$$a_{i,1}, a_{i,2}, \\ldots, a_{i,m}$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_{i,j} \\lt 2^{20}$$$) — description of the matrix $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$(n^2 + m^2)$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$500$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single integer $$$b$$$ — the smallest possible $$$\\textit{beauty}$$$ of the matrix."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n1 2\n1 3\n2 3\n0 1 0\n5 4 4\n2 3\n0 2 4\n4 5 1\n3 3\n1 2 3\n4 5 6\n7 8 9\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n3\n13\n24\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's denote $$$r(i)$$$ as the first type operation applied on the $$$i$$$-th row, and $$$c(j)$$$ as the second type operation applied on the $$$j$$$-th column."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, you can apply an operation $$$c(1)$$$, which assigns $$$a_{1,1} := 1 \\oplus 3 = 2$$$. Then, we'll receive this matrix: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, you can apply an operation $$$r(1)$$$, which assigns: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_{1,1} := g(1) = 0 \\oplus 5 = 5$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_{1,2} := g(2) = 1 \\oplus 4 = 5$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_{1,3} := g(3) = 0 \\oplus 4 = 4$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The resulting matrix after performing the operation is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"5"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"5"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"5"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, the best way to achieve minimum $$$\\textit{beauty}$$$ is applying three operations: $$$c(3)$$$, $$$r(2)$$$, and $$$c(2)$$$. The resulting matrix is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"6"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"5"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"6"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1993E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1993/problem/E"}